<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  muEmbed_OO200.xml: lightflavorspectra_OO200/submodule/MuDstProcessEmbedding

  Ported from lightflavorspectra_etof/submodule/MuDstProcessEmbedding/muEmbed_Collider.xml
  (that file is itself energy-agnostic: it's parameterized by &energy;/&part;/&requestID;/
  &starver; entities filled in by runSchedSubmission_OO200.bash's star-submit-template call).

  WHAT CHANGED FROM THE ORIGINAL, AND WHY:
    - The only real content change needed is the hardcoded /star/data03/... paths below,
      which were the ORIGINAL AUTHOR's (harasty's) personal RCF scratch/pwg directories.
      Filled in with Andrew's RCF username (liggett2820) 2026-08-06, replacing every
      /star/data03/scratch/.../liggett2820/... and /star/data03/pwg/.../liggett2820/...
      path below. runSchedSubmission_OO200.bash's $OutputDir matches the
      <output>/<stdout>/<stderr> URLs here: if you ever change one, change both.
    - Left the &energy;/&part;/&requestID;/&starver;/&filesPerProcess;/&nFiles;/&motherID;
      entities as-is: these get filled in per-job by star-submit-template, driven by
      runSchedSubmission_OO200.bash. &motherID; is passed as 0 here (this template is for
      the plain TPC-efficiency embedding, not hybrid feed-down, which needs its own
      mother-ID-bearing request/template, not ported yet; see compile.bash's header note).
    - Added 2026-09-02: <shell> line below, matching the one already added to
      xml/runPicoBinner_OO200_SDCC_template.xml for the same reason (see that file's own
      header comment). SDCC's farm/worker nodes have moved to AlmaLinux 9, but STAR's
      official software (root4star included) still needs the old SL7 environment, so the
      job's own <command> now runs inside the SL7-compatible singularity container on
      whatever worker node picks it up, the same way compile.bash needed it wrapped
      around `cons` at the terminal. This file had no <shell> line at all before; worth
      double-checking after the first job runs that this was actually the missing piece,
      since it wasn't verified by an actual failed/succeeded submission before adding it.
    - RESOLVED 2026-09-09: the &starver; gap flagged above was a real bug, confirmed at
      RCF. Without an explicit `starver &starver;` call, the job's csh session picked up
      whatever STAR_LEVEL its login shell defaults to (observed to be SL24c on the actual
      worker node, via the library search path in a job's own dlopen diagnostic), not the
      SL23c this repo's StMuAnalysisMaker_OO200.so/bin_temp/*.so are compiled against.
      Fixed by adding `starver &starver;` as the first line of <command>, matching the
      reference lightflavorspectra_etof/.../muEmbed_Collider.xml this file was ported from
      (that file already has `starver &starver;` as its first <command> line; this
      repo's port had silently dropped it). This was a real, independently-confirmed
      fix (before/after comparison of the job's own library search path showed SL24c
      paths disappear and SL23c paths appear), but it turned out NOT to be the cause of
      the setOutputName crash below; that crash persisted identically after this fix
      too. Keeping this fix regardless; see 2026-09-11 note for the actual cause.

    - RESOLVED 2026-09-11: the real cause of
      `Error: Can't call StMuAnalysisMaker::setOutputName(a_outputFileName) in current
      scope` (followed by a segfault) was a NAME COLLISION: this repo's own custom
      StMuAnalysisMaker Maker class shares its name with a real, generic example Maker
      that ships as part of STAR's official software distribution
      (/star/nfs4/AFS/star/packages/SL23c/.sl73_x8664_gcc485/lib/StMuAnalysisMaker.so),
      which lacks the setOutputName(string) method this repo's version defines. On the
      worker node, gSystem->Load("StMuAnalysisMaker") was resolving to STAR's official
      library instead of this repo's own; confirmed via a one-off diagnostic print of
      the loaded class's GetDeclFileName() and gSystem->GetLibraries() in doMuDst.C,
      which showed the official SL23c packages path, not this repo's own StRoot path.
      A SECOND, independent bug made this worse: this repo's own compiled Maker library
      was never actually being shipped to the worker node in the SandBox zip AT ALL, in
      any submission, ever; the <SandBox> <File> list below referenced
      `./.sl73_gcc485`, but `cons` (via compile.bash) actually builds into
      `.sl73_x8664_gcc485` (note the missing _x8664). SUMS's own packaging step silently
      warned "The existence of the file or directory './.sl73_gcc485' could not be
      validated" and skipped it on every single submission, meaning gSystem->Load() on
      the worker could only ever find STAR's official same-named Maker, never this
      repo's own, regardless of any renaming. Fixed two ways together: (1) renamed the
      class, its source directory, AND its source files all to StMuAnalysisMaker_OO200
      (class name, file basename, and StRoot/ subdirectory name must all three match for
      `cons`'s Conscript-standard build + gSystem->Load(bare name) to resolve correctly),
      and (2) corrected the <SandBox> <File> entry below to `./.sl73_x8664_gcc485`, so
      the compiled Maker library actually reaches the worker node now. Also fixed the
      downstream hadd/output step: the <command> block's
      `source /afs/rhic.bnl.gov/star/ROOT/6.20.08/build/bin/thisroot.csh` line pointed at
      a path that does not exist at this site at all; removed it and pointed `hadd`
      directly at the one already provided by `starver &starver;`'s own
      $ROOTSYS/bin (confirmed it supports the `-f6` flag the <command> block wants). Confirmed the
      full fix end-to-end with a 16-file test job (requestID 20232003, part=pip):
      DIAG prints showed the class loading from this repo's own StRoot path, the run
      completed "Finished Event Loop"/"Completed Finish() with total number of events
      16783" (previously 0), zero StChain errors, and a real non-empty
      muEmbed_*_f6.root landed in the destination directory with real histograms and an
      eventTree inside. NOTE FOR FUTURE SUBMISSIONS: star-submit-template caches the
      SandBox zip (MuDstEmbeddingPackage_pi_K_p_OO200_200.zip) and does NOT always
      rebuild it fresh; confirmed empirically that two consecutive submissions after
      fixes above kept failing identically (shipping a stale pre-fix zip) until the zip
      was manually `rm -f`'d. Always delete that zip before resubmitting whenever
      doMuDst.C, StRoot/, .sl73_x8664_gcc485/, headers/, submodule/, bin_temp/, or
      makefile_toggles.h change, even if SUMS does not warn you.
    - FIXED 2026-09-02: this whole comment block (both the pre-existing text above and
      the <shell>/&starver; notes just added above it) used a double hyphen as an em
      dash throughout. XML comments cannot contain that two-character sequence anywhere
      inside them (only as part of the closing delimiter), and star-submit-template
      enforces that strictly: the very first submission attempt against this file failed
      for all six species with a "string not permitted within comments" parse error.
      Every double-hyphen in this comment (old and new) has been replaced with a colon,
      semicolon, or plain period instead.
-->
<job maxFilesPerProcess="&filesPerProcess;" fileListSyntax="paths" copyInputLocally="true">

  <shell>singularity exec -e -B /direct -B /star -B /afs -B /gpfs -B /sdcc/lustre02 /cvmfs/star.sdcc.bnl.gov/containers/rhic_sl7.sif</shell>

  <Generator>
    <Location>/star/data03/scratch/liggett2820/tmp/muEmb/</Location>
  </Generator>

  <command>
        starver &starver;
        root4star -q -b doMuDst.C\(\"$FILELIST\",\"muEmbed_${JOBID}.root\",\"&part;\",1000000000,&motherID;\)
        hadd -f6 ${SCRATCH}/muEmbed_${JOBID}_f6.root ${SCRATCH}/muEmbed_${JOBID}.root
        mv ${SCRATCH}/muEmbed_${JOBID}_f6.root /star/data03/pwg/liggett2820/embedding/&part;/&energy;_&requestID;/muEmbed_${JOBID}_f6.root
        rm ${SCRATCH}/muEmbed_${JOBID}_f6.root
        rm ${SCRATCH}/muEmbed_${JOBID}.root
  </command>

  <SandBox installer="ZIP">
        <Package name="MuDstEmbeddingPackage_pi_K_p_OO200_&energy;">
              	<File>file:./doMuDst.C</File>
	 	<File>file:./StRoot</File>
		<File>file:./.sl73_x8664_gcc485</File>
                <File>file:./headers</File>
                <File>file:./submodule</File>
                <File>file:./bin_temp</File>
                <File>file:./makefile_toggles.h</File>
        </Package>
  </SandBox>

  <input URL="filelist:&filelistdir;/&energy;GeV_&part;_&requestID;.list" nFiles="&nFiles;" />
  <stdout URL="file:/star/data03/scratch/liggett2820/tmp/muEmb/&energy;_&part;_&requestID;_$JOBID.out"/>
  <stderr URL="file:/star/data03/scratch/liggett2820/tmp/muEmb/&energy;_&part;_&requestID;_$JOBID.err"/>
  <output fromScratch="*.root" toURL="file:/star/data03/pwg/liggett2820/embedding/&part;/&energy;_&requestID;/" />
  <output fromScratch="*.txt" toURL="file:/star/data03/pwg/liggett2820/embedding/&part;/&energy;_&requestID;/" />
</job>
